Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-22-2000||02:42 PM||||I don't know if this will post twice.<BR>This is a question that has come up before, but I can't do a search right now.<BR>With the v8 in my car now (It's carbed).<BR>I put a new edelbrock 600 on the car to avoid (I thought) just this problem.  When I go around a corner and then accelerate I get a real jerky hesitation when I step on the gas.  My mechanic buddy got around this on his car by rotating the carb to face forward on the car.  I'm not sure what type of carb he has. I know it has something to do with the gas reserve in the floats but am wondering what I might do about this.  I also thought that using the electric fuel pump (at 61/2 lbs) would keep everything steady.  It's not a real big deal but annoying. Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-22-2000||02:56 PM||||Ive read that before with offroad trucks, your suppose to adjust the float level in the carb, im pretty sure you have to raise it||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-22-2000||06:21 PM||||does sound like a float not set right. Could also be the fuel getting away from the tank pickup if it's low on gas.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||11-22-2000||07:32 PM||||That carb should be getting 4.5lb of fuel pressure. Lower your fuel pressure to 4.5 lb. and see if that cures the bog. If it doesn't your going to need to lower your float level.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||11-22-2000||10:19 PM||||Thanks guys, I'm going in to the shop on Sat to reset timing and adjust valves so will check floats and try resetting fuel pressure.  My mileage was good at first but sucks big time right now.  Still fast as can be.  Not had anyone give any pressure on the road yet (not that I would speed or anything like that, honest).  The ricers crack me up though, they come up beside me on the freeway and try to cut me off but I just tap the gas and am by them before they know what's happened.  Then they come flying by a few seconds later as if to say "I won, I passed you" Lame.||||reg||14
Z||000005||gixxer||11-23-2000||10:55 AM||||Never deviate from the specified float level. Just be sure that the fuel pressure is appropriate for the carb.||||reg||1
